IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cbr-nouns`
IMPORT `cbr-seat`

-- Child Benefit (Rates) Regulations 2006 -- WORKED CASES OF THE SEAT LAYER (cbr-seat.l4).
--
-- Each case is a person in the seat asking one of the seat's questions with the facts
-- that person could state. Every expected value is written here from the text, with
-- its reason beside it; none is copied from the encoding's output. The cases marked
-- FORK assert the reading taken where the text does not settle which provision
-- prevails (NOTES.md, forks F1 to F3 and F8): a reviewer who reads the text the other
-- way sees at once which assertions change.
--
-- The people:
--   Priya        a lone parent, one child Asha (born 15 March 2015), later a second, Dev.
--   Mary         Asha's grandmother, who lives with Asha's mother.
--   Tom          Asha's stepfather, who lives with Asha's mother as her spouse.
--   Ana and Ben  a married couple, each paid for a child (Ana's born 10 January 2012,
--                Ben's born 5 February 2014).
--   Cal and Dee  partners, each paid for a child born on 7 October 2016.
--   Chidi        a member of a polygamous marriage lived in together.
--   Eve          lives with her husband and, otherwise than as a couple, with a child's parent.
--
-- Every case file call names every input (`WITH`), so a case can be read against the
-- question's `@desc`s.

§ `Worked cases of the seat layer`

-- a week of 2026: Are these Regulations in force for my week
-- reg 1(1): 1 June 2026 is after 10 April 2006.
#ASSERT (`Are these Regulations in force for my week` WITH `the first day of the week` IS (Date 1 6 2026))

-- the day before commencement: Are these Regulations in force for my week
-- reg 1(1): the Regulations come into force on 10 April 2006, so a week beginning on the 9th is before.
#ASSERT NOT (`Are these Regulations in force for my week` WITH `the first day of the week` IS (Date 9 4 2006))

-- the first day of commencement: Are these Regulations in force for my week
-- reg 1(1): 10 April 2006 itself.
#ASSERT (`Are these Regulations in force for my week` WITH `the first day of the week` IS (Date 10 4 2006))

-- a young person in Great Britain: Is the young person a qualifying young person
-- reg 1(2)(a): in Great Britain and such a person for Part 9 of SSCBA.
#ASSERT (`Is the young person a qualifying young person` WITH `where the young person is` IS `in Great Britain`, `the young person is a qualifying young person under Part 9` IS TRUE)

-- a young person in Northern Ireland: Is the young person a qualifying young person
-- reg 1(2)(b).
#ASSERT (`Is the young person a qualifying young person` WITH `where the young person is` IS `in Northern Ireland`, `the young person is a qualifying young person under Part 9` IS TRUE)

-- a young person elsewhere: Is the young person a qualifying young person
-- reg 1(2): neither limb reaches a person who is in neither place.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the young person a qualifying young person` WITH `where the young person is` IS `in neither Great Britain nor Northern Ireland`, `the young person is a qualifying young person under Part 9` IS TRUE)

-- a young person who is not one under Part 9: Is the young person a qualifying young person
-- reg 1(2)(a): not such a person for the purposes of Part 9.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the young person a qualifying young person` WITH `where the young person is` IS `in Great Britain`, `the young person is a qualifying young person under Part 9` IS FALSE)

-- a week beginning Monday 8 June 2026: On what day are the facts tested for my week
-- reg 1(3): the facts are those existing at the beginning of that week.
#ASSERT (`On what day are the facts tested for my week` WITH `the first day of the week` IS (Date 8 6 2026)) EQUALS (Date 8 6 2026)

-- Priya, a lone parent, for her only child Asha: Which case under regulation 2(1) applies to this child
-- reg 2(1)(a): the only person in respect of whom child benefit is payable to her.
#ASSERT (`Which case under regulation 2(1) applies to this child` WITH `the first day of the week` IS (Date 1 6 2026), `child benefit is payable to me for this child` IS TRUE, `the child's date of birth` IS (Date 15 3 2015), `the person I claim for is a child` IS TRUE, `where the young person is` IS `in Great Britain`, `the young person is a qualifying young person under Part 9` IS FALSE, `this is the only or the eldest child I am paid child benefit for` IS TRUE, `I live with a parent of the child` IS FALSE, `I live with that parent as mentioned in regulation 2(2)(a)` IS FALSE, `I am a voluntary organisation` IS FALSE, `I live with my spouse or civil partner` IS FALSE, `I live with another person as my spouse or civil partner` IS FALSE, `a party to my marriage is married to more than one person` IS FALSE, `my marriage ceremony took place under the law of a country which permits polygamy` IS FALSE, `I live with the other members of my marriage` IS FALSE, `child benefit would be payable at the enhanced rate to someone else in my household` IS FALSE, `the date of birth of the eldest of the children they would be paid the enhanced rate for` IS (Date 1 1 2000), `the kind of payment I am paid for the week` IS `a payment of some other kind`, `receiving it entitles me to an increase for dependants listed in Schedule 4` IS FALSE, `the instrument the allowance is granted under` IS `an instrument not listed in paragraph (6)(c)(i) to (vii)`, `the Commissioners accept it as analogous to a listed allowance` IS FALSE, `the payment is paid to me for the week` IS FALSE, `the payment is paid for this child` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST `the case for the enhanced rate`

-- Priya, for her second child Dev: Which case under regulation 2(1) applies to this child
-- reg 2(1)(b): not the only, elder or eldest, so any other case.
#ASSERT (`Which case under regulation 2(1) applies to this child` WITH `the first day of the week` IS (Date 1 6 2026), `child benefit is payable to me for this child` IS TRUE, `the child's date of birth` IS (Date 2 9 2018), `the person I claim for is a child` IS TRUE, `where the young person is` IS `in Great Britain`, `the young person is a qualifying young person under Part 9` IS FALSE, `this is the only or the eldest child I am paid child benefit for` IS FALSE, `I live with a parent of the child` IS FALSE, `I live with that parent as mentioned in regulation 2(2)(a)` IS FALSE, `I am a voluntary organisation` IS FALSE, `I live with my spouse or civil partner` IS FALSE, `I live with another person as my spouse or civil partner` IS FALSE, `a party to my marriage is married to more than one person` IS FALSE, `my marriage ceremony took place under the law of a country which permits polygamy` IS FALSE, `I live with the other members of my marriage` IS FALSE, `child benefit would be payable at the enhanced rate to someone else in my household` IS FALSE, `the date of birth of the eldest of the children they would be paid the enhanced rate for` IS (Date 1 1 2000), `the kind of payment I am paid for the week` IS `a payment of some other kind`, `receiving it entitles me to an increase for dependants listed in Schedule 4` IS FALSE, `the instrument the allowance is granted under` IS `an instrument not listed in paragraph (6)(c)(i) to (vii)`, `the Commissioners accept it as analogous to a listed allowance` IS FALSE, `the payment is paid to me for the week` IS FALSE, `the payment is paid for this child` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST `any other case`

-- Priya, for Asha: What weekly amount of child benefit is payable for this child
-- reg 2(1)(a): the enhanced rate is £27.05.
#ASSERT (`What weekly amount of child benefit is payable for this child` WITH `the first day of the week` IS (Date 1 6 2026), `child benefit is payable to me for this child` IS TRUE, `the child's date of birth` IS (Date 15 3 2015), `the person I claim for is a child` IS TRUE, `where the young person is` IS `in Great Britain`, `the young person is a qualifying young person under Part 9` IS FALSE, `this is the only or the eldest child I am paid child benefit for` IS TRUE, `I live with a parent of the child` IS FALSE, `I live with that parent as mentioned in regulation 2(2)(a)` IS FALSE, `I am a voluntary organisation` IS FALSE, `I live with my spouse or civil partner` IS FALSE, `I live with another person as my spouse or civil partner` IS FALSE, `a party to my marriage is married to more than one person` IS FALSE, `my marriage ceremony took place under the law of a country which permits polygamy` IS FALSE, `I live with the other members of my marriage` IS FALSE, `child benefit would be payable at the enhanced rate to someone else in my household` IS FALSE, `the date of birth of the eldest of the children they would be paid the enhanced rate for` IS (Date 1 1 2000), `the kind of payment I am paid for the week` IS `a payment of some other kind`, `receiving it entitles me to an increase for dependants listed in Schedule 4` IS FALSE, `the instrument the allowance is granted under` IS `an instrument not listed in paragraph (6)(c)(i) to (vii)`, `the Commissioners accept it as analogous to a listed allowance` IS FALSE, `the payment is paid to me for the week` IS FALSE, `the payment is paid for this child` IS FALSE, `the earlier rates with the 1998 savings would have given me an amount` IS FALSE, `the weekly amount the earlier rates would have given me` IS 0) EQUALS JUST 27.05

-- Priya, for Dev: What weekly amount of child benefit is payable for this child
